.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
See the module.
.PP
\fBStepper\fR: a sequence of steps with the current one's content, after Mantine's \fBStepper\fR. The behavior (statuses from \fBactive\fR, click rules, next / back, connector fill) is \fBprimitives::stepper\fR; this widget is its look.
.PP
Controlled: the app owns \fBactive\fR (\fB0..steps\fR, or \fBsteps\fR for the completed screen) and moves it from \fBon_step_click\fR and its own Back / Next buttons.
.PP
.nf
.RS
// state: `step: usize` (see `StepperState` for next / prev / goto)
Stepper::new()
    .active(self.step)
    .on_step_click(Msg::Step)
    .allow_next_steps_select(false)
    .step(StepperStep::new("Account").description("Name and password").content(|| account()))
    .step(StepperStep::new("Verify").loading(self.checking).content(|| verify()))
    .step(StepperStep::new("Done"))
    .completed(|| text("All set").into())     // shown when active == 3
.RE
.fi
.IP \(bu 2
a step's circle shows its number, its \fBicon\fR, a check (or its \fBcompleted_icon\fR), an error mark (\fBinvalid\fR), or a loading mark (\fBloading\fR); the lines between steps fill with the accent up to the active step;
.IP \(bu 2
\fBhorizontal\fR puts the steps in a row with the content of the active step below; \fBvertical\fR stacks them, the line running down beside the active step's content;
.IP \(bu 2
only the active step's content closure is called;
.IP \(bu 2
on a narrow width a horizontal stepper \fBcollapse\fRs to the current step's label (the others keep their circle), or, with \fBwrap\fR, flows onto several lines;
.IP \(bu 2
\fBstatuses\fR and \fBclickable\fR replace the derived statuses and click rules (a \fBForm\fR gives its own: see \fBStepIndicator\fR).
